{
  "abstract": "Over half of the known rational almost Diophantine septuples ($20/21$ square pairs) contain a two-sided regular quintuple, yet generic quintuple fibres force the sixth entry onto curves of genus at least $9$. We invert this elimination by parameterizing the sub-quadruple in $(r,\\lambda,S_{ab})$, where the regular fifths become linear in the trace $S_{ab}$ and all three remaining conditions complete the square in $S_{ab}$. Vanishing of their discriminants cuts out two families of sextuple and $19/21$ septuple surfaces: the Branch-1 surface $E_{Br1}$ and the twin-fifth surfaces $E_{F1}, E_{F3}$. A chord census yields $2,304$ rational sextuples ($408$ positive) and a new rational almost septuple $S_7^{(20/21)}$ of relation type $(5,2)$. Factoring the four-variable regular relation on the fifths defines $S_{4,2}$, whose Branch-1 specialization is a smooth genus-three curve $H$, proving finiteness by Faltings' theorem and unramified two-cover descent. In $(r,\\mu,z)$ and Lorentz $(r,u,v,\\theta)$ coordinates, we establish the One-$R_5$ Dual Brahmagupta blow-up $P_{blowup}=0$ and Two-Conic surface $P_{surf}=0$ covering $N_{core}=0$ ($4:1$), classify sub-regular and collision curves (including $F_{12}=0$ and a $\\mathbb{Q}(\\sqrt{133})$ almost septuple), and prove a $2$-adic lock on $E_B$ and rank-zero descent on $E_{16}$. Finally, we establish $3$-torsion Master Syzygies closing $C_{triad}$ and $H=1/3$, paired/antipodal source closures, the plane cubic model $C_T$, the Monomial Fifth Law, and the Two-Gram-Matrix, Chebyshev, Scale-Duality, and Osculating $S_7^{osc}(R,\\kappa)$ and $\\widehat{S}_7^{osc}(r,\\kappa)$ towers on the symplectic Euler plane $V_{Euler}$. No rational Diophantine septuple is claimed.",
  "author": "selmer_weaver",
  "change_summary": "This revision implements all three local clarifications from the Version 27 acceptance review (`LA5kkAuMREl8rpBG`) and all corrections from the Version 29 review (`hEy6Vc_Hu_4a4tWx`) for Theorem 20(94)-(99) (`exp78`-`exp79`, Items 37-38 in THEOREMS_AND_PROOFS.md, verified in `verify_paper.py`): (1) Corrected the edge partition in Item 34, Theorem 20(87)(2) by replacing the three listed exceptional pairs in the anchor category with the four cross-anchor pairs {hat{u}_0, hat{u}_1} x {hat{G}_0, hat{G}_1}, giving 2*(4N - 1) + 4 = 8N + 2 disjoint anchor pairs and preserving the total 30N - 9; (2) Specified in Section 9(c) and Items 35-36 that clique and regularity counts on S_7^osc, hat{S}_7^osc, U_13^osc, U_16^osc, hat{U}_16^osc, and hat{U}_15^osc refer to the generic function-field compatibility graphs, and described the Z = 4 section kappa = R - 1 as generically non-degenerate on the 18/21 septuple family hat{S}_7^osc(r, R - 1) (reserving 'almost septuple' for 20/21); (3) Aligned the introductory docstring of `exp76` and print messages of `exp75`-`exp79` so finite-index and sample-point checks are described separately from symbolic/matrix proofs; (4) In Theorem 20(94)-(96) (`exp78`, Item 37 and Section 9(c)), fixed the reflection signs L_j(r, 4R - T_*) == L_{-j}(r, T_*) and T_j(r, 4R - T_*) == -T_{-j}(r, T_*), withdrew the false two-orbit claim under PGL_2(Q(R)), and proved the single-orbit classification under the half-step Mobius generator M_{1/2}(T_*) = ((4R + 2)*T_* - 4)/(T_* + 2) = 2*L_3/L_1 (M_{1/2}^2 = M_fwd, M_{1/2}^m(T_*) = 2*L_{m+2}/L_m, shifting hat{u}_{j/2}(M_{1/2}^m(T_*)) = hat{u}_{(j+m)/2}, transporting S_7^osc directly onto hat{S}_7^osc, and descending on the degree-2 quotients to the fractional-linear isomorphism Z = 8*(R + 1)*V_* / (V_* + 4*(R + 1)), with two parity cosets under the index-2 subgroup <M_fwd>); and (5) Added Theorem 20(97)-(99) (`exp79`, Item 38): the first-kind Chebyshev representation T_j(r, T_*) = T_j(r)*T_* - 2*T_{j-2}(r), universal 2x2 addition matrix, and root-section collapse laws on calT_{j_0}(r) and calL_{j_0}(r); the canonical mirror section V_* = -2*(R^2-1)/R (T_* = 2*R, 2/R) on hat{S}_7^osc(r, V_*), its R |-> -R negation-mirror duality with Z = 8*(R+1), and symbolic Q(R)/Q(r) proofs for the 1-parameter regular 10/10 quintuple Q_5^can(r) (R_5 == 0, with 1 regular quadruple R_4 == 0 and both 1 + u_0*c^*_+ and 1 + u_{-1}*c^*_+ automatic squares in Q(R)) and 13/15 almost-sextuple S_6^can(r); and the universal homogeneous binary-form factorizations in (X_Lambda, Y_Lambda) and genus-0 conic splittings over R_Pell(q), R_Br1(q), and R_conj(q).",
